WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:02.000
F56 push/pull paddle prototype, shown in an exploded CAD view.

00:02.000 --> 00:04.000
Two switches and two resistor paths enter the housing.

00:04.000 --> 00:06.000
Two return springs move into place.

00:06.000 --> 00:08.000
RC bearings slide into the moving blade.

00:08.000 --> 00:10.000
The blade lowers onto the housing and spring seats.

00:10.000 --> 00:12.000
Shims, captured nuts and two short pivot screws complete the illustrated assembly.

00:12.000 --> 00:14.000
The middle stays open for access to the original mounting screw.

00:14.000 --> 00:16.000
The shells become transparent to reveal the switches and springs.

00:16.000 --> 00:19.000
Pull. [Illustrative click] The pull channel closes, then opens as the blade returns.

00:19.000 --> 00:20.000
Neutral. Both channels are open.

00:20.000 --> 00:23.000
Push. [Illustrative click] The push channel closes, then opens as the blade returns.

00:23.000 --> 00:25.000
Neutral. Both channels are open again.

00:25.000 --> 00:28.000
P02 CAD prototype. Wheel fit and physical testing are next.
